1
00:00:15,849 --> 00:00:18,018
[engine revving loudly]

2
00:00:20,603 --> 00:00:22,147
[Chrishell] Wow, this is so pretty.

3
00:00:25,942 --> 00:00:28,319
-[Mary] Honey, I'm home.
-[women laughing]

4
00:00:29,154 --> 00:00:30,280
Oh my gosh.

5
00:00:31,823 --> 00:00:33,950
[Mary] That's where I would want to do
the ceremony.

6
00:00:34,034 --> 00:00:35,243
-[Chrishell] Yes.
-[Mary] Right?

7
00:00:35,326 --> 00:00:36,786
Yeah, on that beach.

8
00:00:37,037 --> 00:00:39,956
[Mary] I've been having a terrible time 
booking a wedding venue,

9
00:00:40,040 --> 00:00:41,916
but this other agent, Shawn,

10
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:44,294
offered me a 35 million dollar 
house in Malibu.

11
00:00:44,627 --> 00:00:47,589
So if I get this, it's going to be epic.

12
00:00:47,672 --> 00:00:49,007
Shawn?

13
00:00:49,090 --> 00:00:50,383
[Shawn] I gotta call you back.

14
00:00:51,217 --> 00:00:53,011
-Hi, Mary. Good to see you.
-Good to see you.

15
00:00:53,094 --> 00:00:54,262
Oh. Mwah.

16
00:00:55,221 --> 00:00:56,890
[Mary] So I brought reinforcements,

17
00:00:56,973 --> 00:00:58,683
'cause we're making it be here.

18
00:00:58,767 --> 00:01:00,643
-Thank you for having us.
-My pleasure.

19
00:01:00,727 --> 00:01:03,188
[Mary] A lot of people in LA
have second homes.

20
00:01:03,271 --> 00:01:07,317
The owners of this Malibu house
don't fully occupy it.

21
00:01:07,400 --> 00:01:10,236
So Shawn is definitely doing me a favor

22
00:01:10,320 --> 00:01:13,990
by talking to his clients
and getting this as my wedding venue.

23
00:01:14,074 --> 00:01:17,077
Plus, they're willing to work 
within my budget. Thank God.

24
00:01:17,160 --> 00:01:18,912
It is such a weight off my shoulders.

25
00:01:18,995 --> 00:01:20,580
-Oh.
-[Amanza] I just saw a dolphin.

26
00:01:20,663 --> 00:01:22,499
-[Mary] Did you?
-Did you seriously?

27
00:01:22,582 --> 00:01:24,834
[Mary] You said that, 
that you see them sometimes.

28
00:01:24,918 --> 00:01:27,128
-[Shawn] The wildlife here is crazy.
-Gorgeous.

29
00:01:27,212 --> 00:01:29,964
Let me take you on a tour of this house,
I want you to see all of it.

30
00:01:39,057 --> 00:01:40,892
[Shawn] This is the main living area.

31
00:01:40,975 --> 00:01:45,730
This outside area, I mean,
you could have cocktail hour out here.

32
00:01:46,106 --> 00:01:47,816
[Chrishell] Ooh, yeah, that'd be nice.

33
00:01:47,899 --> 00:01:49,776
Girls, oh my god,
can you imagine?

34
00:01:49,859 --> 00:01:51,694
[Mary] Everyone standing around like...

35
00:01:52,320 --> 00:01:54,155
-[Shawn] Come this way.
-[Mary] Alright.

36
00:01:54,781 --> 00:01:57,033
-[Amanza] It just keeps going.
-[Chrishell] I know.

37
00:01:57,116 --> 00:01:59,494
-[Mary] There's so much potential.
-Oh, it wraps around.

38
00:01:59,577 --> 00:02:01,037
[Shawn] How beautiful is this?

39
00:02:01,121 --> 00:02:02,288
-[Mary] Yes.
-[Amanza] Wow.

40
00:02:02,372 --> 00:02:07,168
[Mary] This would be such a gorgeous spot 
for the reception, you're right.

41
00:02:07,252 --> 00:02:09,796
[Shawn] A hundred percent, 
and you have great neighbors.

42
00:02:09,879 --> 00:02:12,006
You've got Flea
from Red Hot Chili Peppers.

43
00:02:12,090 --> 00:02:12,924
Yeah?

44
00:02:13,007 --> 00:02:15,718
[Shawn] Best of all,
you've got Lady Gaga up there.

45
00:02:16,219 --> 00:02:19,055
I mean... I gotta take this call.

46
00:02:19,138 --> 00:02:20,431
Enjoy the property a little bit.

47
00:02:20,515 --> 00:02:22,475
I'll pick up with you guys
and show you the beach.

48
00:02:22,559 --> 00:02:23,434
-Okay.
-Thank you.

49
00:02:25,395 --> 00:02:29,566
The thing is, I wanted the destination
wedding so much and that's just like...

50
00:02:30,275 --> 00:02:31,860
Logistically, it's not going to happen.

51
00:02:31,943 --> 00:02:35,029
So this is like,
I feel like I'm on vacation right now.

52
00:02:35,113 --> 00:02:36,281
-Exactly.
-Me too.

53
00:02:36,364 --> 00:02:38,700
I think so, too.
That's exactly how ours was.

54
00:02:38,783 --> 00:02:40,702
Because it was in Malibu,

55
00:02:40,785 --> 00:02:43,746
it was like a destination
without it needing to be destination.

56
00:02:43,830 --> 00:02:46,833
-[Amanza] I got married in Indiana and...
-[women laughing]

57
00:02:46,916 --> 00:02:49,711
...it wasn't very romantic
that weekend, remember?

58
00:02:49,794 --> 00:02:50,670
Oh my god!

59
00:02:51,087 --> 00:02:55,049
I really do not want to talk
about Amanza's wedding.

60
00:02:55,466 --> 00:02:57,552
Mary got food poisoning the night before.

61
00:02:57,635 --> 00:02:59,888
She had eaten something sus in Indiana,

62
00:02:59,971 --> 00:03:03,558
and she had to leave, like,
I think halfway through the reception.

63
00:03:03,641 --> 00:03:06,269
She was like shitting
and throwing her brains out.

64
00:03:06,561 --> 00:03:07,729
[chuckling]

65
00:03:07,812 --> 00:03:11,024
Too bad we don't have something to cheers 
your new wedding venue now.

66
00:03:11,107 --> 00:03:13,776
We'll have to save it
for when you're getting hitched.

67
00:03:13,860 --> 00:03:14,777
Yes, oh my god.

68
00:03:14,861 --> 00:03:16,654
Now we just got to get your dress.

69
00:03:16,738 --> 00:03:18,781
[Chrishell] The guest list,
how's that coming along?

70
00:03:18,865 --> 00:03:20,325
I talked to Romain last night.

71
00:03:20,408 --> 00:03:22,785
-He's still adamant.
-[Chrishell] He's not budging.

72
00:03:22,869 --> 00:03:26,414
But I'm not gonna let 
Davina come between us.

73
00:03:26,497 --> 00:03:29,000
You know, we're getting married,
we're happy.

74
00:03:29,083 --> 00:03:32,462
I just think, like, rip it off
like a Band-Aid and tell her

75
00:03:32,545 --> 00:03:36,090
because it's going to make it
much better once you

76
00:03:36,174 --> 00:03:38,009
just get that stress off your plate.

77
00:03:38,092 --> 00:03:39,719
[Amanza] Couldn't she just come?

78
00:03:39,802 --> 00:03:41,638
You wouldn't even see her,
this place is so big.

79
00:03:41,721 --> 00:03:44,307
You could just stick her up
on one of the balconies,

80
00:03:44,766 --> 00:03:46,267
and give her some binoculars.

81
00:03:46,351 --> 00:03:48,061
Put her in time out over there.

82
00:03:48,144 --> 00:03:49,145
Time out!

83
00:03:49,687 --> 00:03:55,234
This fight with Davina is causing
so much strain on my relationship.

84
00:03:55,318 --> 00:03:59,238
I cannot wait for this wedding to be over,
where I can just

85
00:03:59,614 --> 00:04:03,201
settle down and and go back 
to selling real estate.

86
00:04:12,961 --> 00:04:15,713
♪ You chewed me up
Took me for granted ♪

87
00:04:16,839 --> 00:04:19,676
♪ You couldn't see what I could do ♪

88
00:04:19,968 --> 00:04:23,930
♪ I'm a fighter
And I'm feeling you ♪

89
00:04:24,013 --> 00:04:25,723
♪ With some love to prove ♪

90
00:04:25,807 --> 00:04:30,311
♪ Coming back, I'm giving back
And I'm stronger ♪

91
00:04:30,395 --> 00:04:31,813
♪ No, I won't give in ♪

92
00:04:31,896 --> 00:04:34,148
♪ So much confidence ♪

93
00:04:34,232 --> 00:04:35,650
♪ Coming back... ♪

94
00:04:37,318 --> 00:04:39,612
[Christine] I'm so excited
to show you this house.

95
00:04:39,696 --> 00:04:41,322
-[man] Oh, yeah.
-[woman] Looks good.

96
00:04:41,406 --> 00:04:42,782
[Christine] Hello!

97
00:04:42,865 --> 00:04:44,117
[Chrishell] Hey, guys.

98
00:04:44,200 --> 00:04:46,536
-Come on in.
-I want you to meet my clients.

99
00:04:46,619 --> 00:04:49,706
-This is Max and Sepi.
-Hi, how are you. Pleasure to meet you.

100
00:04:49,789 --> 00:04:50,999
Hi, I'm Max. Nice to meet you.

101
00:04:51,082 --> 00:04:53,626
[Christine] They've been looking
for a family-friendly home.

102
00:04:53,710 --> 00:04:55,294
I hope this is the one.

103
00:04:55,420 --> 00:04:58,840
[Chrishell] Okay, this house is
just under 6,400 square feet,

104
00:04:58,923 --> 00:05:00,341
so there's lots of space.

105
00:05:08,099 --> 00:05:10,643
[Chrishell] Huge master,
lots of bedrooms, five in total.

106
00:05:10,727 --> 00:05:12,145
-And you have a yard.
-Yes!

107
00:05:12,228 --> 00:05:13,062
-Amazing.
-Great.

108
00:05:17,233 --> 00:05:19,277
Look around, let her know
if you have any questions.

109
00:05:19,360 --> 00:05:20,862
-Awesome, thank you.
-Absolutely.

110
00:05:20,945 --> 00:05:22,363
[gasps] Gorgeous house.

111
00:05:22,447 --> 00:05:25,366
-I know, it's really pretty, right?
-[Christine] A house of this size,

112
00:05:25,450 --> 00:05:26,909
it's so hard to come by.

113
00:05:26,993 --> 00:05:28,494
-[Sepi] Nice guest bedroom.
-Mm-hmm.

114
00:05:28,578 --> 00:05:31,914
The only thing I'm worried about
is the levels with small kids.

115
00:05:31,998 --> 00:05:34,083
[Sepi] We'd have to put a gate
for the kids.

116
00:05:34,167 --> 00:05:35,126
-Yeah.
-[dog barks]

117
00:05:35,209 --> 00:05:37,211
Oh, and the dog barking.

118
00:05:37,295 --> 00:05:38,296
I noticed that.

119
00:05:38,379 --> 00:05:40,214
Can you imagine losing a deal
because of that?

120
00:05:40,298 --> 00:05:42,550
I've lost deals 'cause of stupider shit.

121
00:05:42,633 --> 00:05:43,885
[Christine laughing]

122
00:05:43,968 --> 00:05:46,346
I can't believe I might miss out 
on selling this house

123
00:05:46,429 --> 00:05:49,349
because of the neighbor's dog,
it won't stop barking.

124
00:05:49,432 --> 00:05:52,185
-[dog barking]
-[Christine] So, what did you guys think?

125
00:05:52,268 --> 00:05:53,269
You love it?

126
00:05:53,353 --> 00:05:55,354
[Max] It's cool. Decent size, too.

127
00:05:55,438 --> 00:05:58,941
Do you guys want to see the outside
where you'd be laying with the kids?

128
00:05:59,025 --> 00:05:59,984
Let me show you.

129
00:06:00,485 --> 00:06:02,070
[Sepi] See how much green we have.

130
00:06:02,487 --> 00:06:03,905
[Christine] Look at the view, Max.

131
00:06:03,988 --> 00:06:06,240
-[Christine] That's perfect for you.
-[Max] There you go.

132
00:06:06,324 --> 00:06:07,784
The Valley views is...

133
00:06:09,077 --> 00:06:12,205
That's like comparing... [laughing]

134
00:06:12,288 --> 00:06:17,085
...Coors Light to Dom Pérignon,
it's just like... It's totally different.

135
00:06:17,168 --> 00:06:18,378
[Chrishell] Artificial grass,

136
00:06:18,461 --> 00:06:20,838
so you don't have to worry,
it's always going to look perfect.

137
00:06:20,922 --> 00:06:22,340
[Christine] I love that.

138
00:06:22,423 --> 00:06:24,300
You've got these pockets completely open

139
00:06:24,383 --> 00:06:25,885
so you've got the indoor-outdoor feel.

140
00:06:25,968 --> 00:06:28,513
This could be an extension
of your living room basically.

141
00:06:28,596 --> 00:06:29,764
[Max] It's really nice.

142
00:06:29,847 --> 00:06:31,390
Thank you so much for showing us.

143
00:06:31,474 --> 00:06:33,309
-Sure, thank you for coming.
-Nice to meet you.

144
00:06:33,393 --> 00:06:34,727
[Max] Thank you for your time.

145
00:06:34,811 --> 00:06:36,771
-[Chrishell] Thank you guys.
-You guys love it?

146
00:06:36,854 --> 00:06:39,273
I love it for you.
Honestly, I really really really do.

147
00:06:39,857 --> 00:06:41,150
I think it's great.

148
00:06:41,234 --> 00:06:44,195
I haven't been getting as many calls
on this house as I expected.

149
00:06:44,278 --> 00:06:49,158
So, I'm really hoping that Christine's
clients are going to think it's perfect

150
00:06:49,242 --> 00:06:51,911
because, honestly, I do think
it'd be really perfect for them.

151
00:06:51,994 --> 00:06:53,830
[Christine] I feel like
they liked the house.

152
00:06:53,913 --> 00:06:55,790
-I know, that's exciting.
-I think they liked it.

153
00:06:55,873 --> 00:06:58,543
This is the first property 
I've showed them that 

154
00:06:58,668 --> 00:07:00,837
they were like, 
"Oh my god, it has a yard."

155
00:07:00,920 --> 00:07:02,004
That's exciting.

156
00:07:02,088 --> 00:07:04,173
Fingers crossed, 
I really want to sell this now.

157
00:07:04,257 --> 00:07:08,886
I mean, can you believe us
working together after last year?

158
00:07:08,970 --> 00:07:11,139
-We have to make this happen.
-That would be amazing.

159
00:07:11,222 --> 00:07:12,306
I'm not gonna lie.

160
00:07:12,390 --> 00:07:15,143
Chrishell and I definitely started off 
on the wrong foot,

161
00:07:15,226 --> 00:07:17,937
but her and I are headed 
in the right direction.

162
00:07:18,020 --> 00:07:20,189
We both can respect 
the value of a dollar.

163
00:07:20,273 --> 00:07:21,983
-For sure!
-The value of a check cashing.

164
00:07:22,066 --> 00:07:23,734
I mean, speaking of checks cashing,

165
00:07:23,818 --> 00:07:26,445
I am like out of my mind trying to plan

166
00:07:26,529 --> 00:07:29,115
the engagement party and everything.
I'm so stressed.

167
00:07:29,198 --> 00:07:31,784
-My gosh, what are you doing?
-I'm not, my party planner's stressed.

168
00:07:31,868 --> 00:07:34,495
Someone's stressed. I don't know. 
Somewhere down the line,

169
00:07:34,579 --> 00:07:35,955
someone's stressed about something.

170
00:07:36,038 --> 00:07:38,791
I didn't plan mine
'cause I feel like it's too stressful.

171
00:07:38,875 --> 00:07:41,377
I feel like the stressful part
is finding the guy,

172
00:07:41,460 --> 00:07:43,796
throwing the party for the guy
should be the fun part.

173
00:07:43,880 --> 00:07:46,632
So I think you should delegate it
to someone else to do.

174
00:07:46,716 --> 00:07:49,051
That's why I feel bad for Mary
because she's so stressed out.

175
00:07:49,135 --> 00:07:51,137
I know, she's planning 
everything on her own.

176
00:07:51,220 --> 00:07:53,055
Well, it's gotta be tough, because

177
00:07:53,139 --> 00:07:55,641
it's obviously super expensive

178
00:07:55,725 --> 00:07:58,436
and it's probably stress on both of them,
and I think that's why

179
00:07:58,519 --> 00:08:00,730
Romain is so sensitive
about Davina coming

180
00:08:00,813 --> 00:08:03,357
because she made that comment
about her paying for everything.

181
00:08:03,441 --> 00:08:04,817
I did not see that coming.

182
00:08:04,901 --> 00:08:06,986
-I didn't know he had that in him.
-No, I didn't.

183
00:08:07,278 --> 00:08:08,446
Like, no way.

184
00:08:08,529 --> 00:08:10,573
I don't want Davina to come to my wedding.

185
00:08:10,656 --> 00:08:11,782
It's done.

186
00:08:12,158 --> 00:08:14,827
[Chrishell] He's always
just so happy-go-lucky.

187
00:08:15,328 --> 00:08:17,288
-What are you doing?
-[imitating Romain] "No!"

188
00:08:17,371 --> 00:08:19,749
Watch someone come in 
while you're doing this.

189
00:08:20,041 --> 00:08:23,586
-She doesn't come with the house.
-"Davina not coming to my wedding."

190
00:08:23,669 --> 00:08:25,421
[Christine] I was like, "What?"

191
00:08:25,505 --> 00:08:27,507
Me and Maya are like, "What'd you say?"

192
00:08:27,590 --> 00:08:28,508
"Davina!"

193
00:08:28,591 --> 00:08:30,510
We're like, "What is he talking about?"

194
00:08:30,593 --> 00:08:31,552
Oh my God.

195
00:08:31,636 --> 00:08:34,013
[Chrishell] Do you even know
what you're gonna do?

196
00:08:34,096 --> 00:08:39,560
So in my mind, picture like
Britney Spears's "Boys" music video.

197
00:08:39,644 --> 00:08:40,478
Okay.

198
00:08:40,561 --> 00:08:43,314
With the LED lights and the table
and the zebras...

199
00:08:43,397 --> 00:08:45,608
-Okay.
-Anyway, I wanna do it like that.

200
00:08:45,691 --> 00:08:49,278
Are you going to have any kind
of zebra skin at your... Please do not.

201
00:08:49,362 --> 00:08:51,656
-What are you talking about?
-You always have furs.

202
00:08:51,739 --> 00:08:53,658
You can't have a zebra
and also have zebra skin.

203
00:08:53,741 --> 00:08:55,535
The zebras are just hanging out.

204
00:08:55,618 --> 00:08:58,704
I feel like you're the kind of person
that would feed chicken to a chicken.

205
00:08:58,788 --> 00:09:00,957
[both laughing]

206
00:09:01,040 --> 00:09:03,209
-Tell me I'm wrong.
-The zebra got paid though.

207
00:09:03,709 --> 00:09:04,669
Oh my God.

208
00:09:04,752 --> 00:09:06,712
He took the check to Bank of America.

209
00:09:06,796 --> 00:09:08,339
I don't think a zebra really wants...

210
00:09:08,422 --> 00:09:11,092
He has a checking and savings account,
a Roth IRA and a CD.

211
00:09:11,550 --> 00:09:14,720
Okay? That zebra is rolling
in the dough, literally.

212
00:09:14,804 --> 00:09:17,473
Christian doesn't have any idea
what I'm spending on this.

213
00:09:18,057 --> 00:09:20,017
Did he give you any kind of guidelines?

214
00:09:20,101 --> 00:09:22,562
Just, "Put it on the tab." There you go.

215
00:09:22,645 --> 00:09:25,606
[Christine] Christian likes
to buy me gifts, that's his thing.

216
00:09:25,690 --> 00:09:27,358
So it works out perfect. [laughing]

217
00:09:27,441 --> 00:09:29,193
[Christine] We don't really talk
about money,

218
00:09:29,277 --> 00:09:32,071
but if I want something,
I have been known to go in his wallet,

219
00:09:32,280 --> 00:09:35,157
get out his American Express,
click to take a picture,

220
00:09:35,241 --> 00:09:36,701
send it to the salesperson.

221
00:09:37,076 --> 00:09:38,411
He has some alerts on his phone.

222
00:09:38,494 --> 00:09:42,248
So I have my Louis Vuitton 
representative on speed dial,

223
00:09:42,331 --> 00:09:43,708
so when he's sleeping...

224
00:09:44,125 --> 00:09:45,418
I'll have her buy a purse 

225
00:09:45,501 --> 00:09:48,879
and then I'll delete the notification 
while he's sleeping. [laughing]

226
00:09:48,963 --> 00:09:51,424
I don't know, some call it fraud,
I call it love.

227
00:09:52,049 --> 00:09:53,593
Whatever. [laughing]

228
00:09:53,676 --> 00:09:55,261
Well, I'm sure it'll be beautiful.

229
00:09:55,386 --> 00:09:56,762
So, you're gonna come, right?

230
00:09:56,846 --> 00:09:58,431
It'll be really fun.

231
00:09:58,514 --> 00:09:59,515
I'm actually... okay.

232
00:09:59,598 --> 00:10:02,852
So I'm glad we get the chance to talk.
I did want to talk to you about this.

233
00:10:02,935 --> 00:10:06,564
I love that you and I've gotten to where
we can work together and we can

234
00:10:06,647 --> 00:10:11,193
maybe have a shared client together
and, you know, it not be so awkward.

235
00:10:11,277 --> 00:10:12,111
But...

236
00:10:12,820 --> 00:10:15,323
I just feel like it's inappropriate 
for me to be there 

237
00:10:15,406 --> 00:10:17,742
and I just, respectfully will decline

238
00:10:17,825 --> 00:10:20,202
because it feels too soon for me.

239
00:10:20,286 --> 00:10:24,832
You and I, only last week,
could be in the same room together.

240
00:10:24,915 --> 00:10:27,793
I don't want it to be awkward.

241
00:10:27,877 --> 00:10:30,963
But then don't you feel like
that's being awkward by not accepting?

242
00:10:31,047 --> 00:10:33,799
I'm cool with being friends with you
with a wall up,

243
00:10:33,924 --> 00:10:35,551
but something like that is like

244
00:10:36,260 --> 00:10:37,970
letting you in again and it scares me.

245
00:10:38,346 --> 00:10:40,222
Well, I'm obviously shocked.

246
00:10:40,306 --> 00:10:43,059
I didn't really realize we were on so...

247
00:10:43,684 --> 00:10:45,144
like, different pages.

248
00:10:45,227 --> 00:10:47,313
I mean, obviously my feelings 
are hurt, but...

249
00:10:47,521 --> 00:10:50,983
[Chrishell] I don't want your feelings 
to be hurt, that's not my goal.

250
00:10:51,067 --> 00:10:52,818
It just seems disingenuous and...

251
00:10:53,944 --> 00:10:56,656
Disingenuous? By me inviting you?

252
00:10:56,739 --> 00:10:58,199
No. For me going.

253
00:10:58,616 --> 00:11:00,868
-Okay.
-It'd be better to have it this way,

254
00:11:01,494 --> 00:11:06,290
than to be at an engagement party with
a couple I've never hung out with once.

255
00:11:06,665 --> 00:11:07,541
He's gonna be like, 

256
00:11:07,625 --> 00:11:10,211
"Who's this bitch? The bitch you 
told me about that you hate?"

257
00:11:10,294 --> 00:11:12,421
And I'm like, "Hey, congratulations!"

258
00:11:12,505 --> 00:11:13,506
I don't hate anyone.

259
00:11:13,589 --> 00:11:15,633
Okay, I hate a few people,
but I don't hate you.

260
00:11:15,716 --> 00:11:19,178
-Okay, but you did. Let's be honest.
-[Christine laughing]

261
00:11:19,261 --> 00:11:21,680
-No.
-And so did I. Let's own it. 

262
00:11:22,223 --> 00:11:23,057
Okay.

263
00:11:23,516 --> 00:11:26,685
And we only just got past that,
so, I'm just saying like...

264
00:11:27,937 --> 00:11:29,230
Eh, baby steps.

265
00:11:51,419 --> 00:11:54,296
[Mary] My clients bought this property
as a flip.

266
00:11:54,380 --> 00:11:58,300
It was bank-owned, they rebuilt it,
and now I'm selling it for him.

267
00:11:58,384 --> 00:12:00,344
And now my newest client Chris

268
00:12:00,428 --> 00:12:03,097
is looking for an investment property
to rent out,

269
00:12:03,180 --> 00:12:05,349
and I think this could be perfect for him.

270
00:12:08,018 --> 00:12:10,396
Hi, how are you?
I didn't even hear you come in.

271
00:12:10,855 --> 00:12:12,565
-Good to see you.
-Good to see you as well.

272
00:12:12,648 --> 00:12:14,191
[Chris] Beautiful pool, my gosh.

273
00:12:14,275 --> 00:12:16,026
-[Mary] Yeah, so this is it.
-It's amazing.

274
00:12:16,110 --> 00:12:17,069
New construction,

275
00:12:17,153 --> 00:12:20,239
and they just completely remodeled it.
Took it down to the studs.

276
00:12:20,656 --> 00:12:22,032
So everything is new.

277
00:12:22,116 --> 00:12:24,368
I'm going to take you
into the master first.

278
00:12:25,202 --> 00:12:27,163
-[Chris] The fireplace is amazing.
-Yeah.

279
00:12:27,246 --> 00:12:28,831
I like how every room leads outdoors.

280
00:12:28,914 --> 00:12:30,624
-And super private.
-Exactly.

281
00:12:30,708 --> 00:12:34,295
Every bedroom, no one can see in.
It's just very private.

282
00:12:38,048 --> 00:12:41,010
It's one story, which is
the main thing you're looking for.

283
00:12:41,427 --> 00:12:42,344
Hey, Mary?

284
00:12:42,428 --> 00:12:43,262
Oh, Jason?

285
00:12:43,345 --> 00:12:45,347
-Hi, Mary.
-[Mary] Hi.

286
00:12:45,765 --> 00:12:48,225
Sorry, I'm just gonna show her around,
I know you're busy.

287
00:12:48,309 --> 00:12:49,518
-Okay.
-You guys have met.

288
00:12:49,602 --> 00:12:50,436
[Mary] Hi.

289
00:12:50,519 --> 00:12:52,646
-Good to see you.
-I didn't know you guys were coming.

290
00:12:52,730 --> 00:12:54,106
-Yeah, sorry.
-Nice to see you.

291
00:12:54,190 --> 00:12:56,150
-Thanks for letting us check it out.
-Of course.

292
00:12:56,233 --> 00:12:57,318
We don't want to interrupt.

293
00:12:57,401 --> 00:12:59,570
-I'm just gonna show her around.
-[Chris] Thank you.

294
00:13:00,279 --> 00:13:01,113
[Mary] Um...

295
00:13:01,197 --> 00:13:04,366
-Sorry, I didn't know that was happening.
-[Chris] No worries at all.

296
00:13:04,450 --> 00:13:05,284
[Chris] No worries.

297
00:13:05,409 --> 00:13:07,912
I can't believe Jason
is crashing my showing.

298
00:13:07,995 --> 00:13:10,831
I'm told they did just under
a million dollars in renovation.

299
00:13:10,915 --> 00:13:13,334
I saw it when they bought it. 
It was just a piece of shit.

300
00:13:13,417 --> 00:13:15,878
So it looks like they did 
a million dollars of work.

301
00:13:15,961 --> 00:13:18,672
[Jason] So, it's a 500 square-foot
guest apartment.

302
00:13:18,798 --> 00:13:20,591
and 2,500 square feet up here.

303
00:13:20,674 --> 00:13:22,176
They added the pool, too. 

304
00:13:22,259 --> 00:13:24,512
The pool wasn't even here,
or the spa before.

305
00:13:25,054 --> 00:13:27,056
-Alright, we'll switch.
-[Mary] Okay. [laughing]

306
00:13:27,139 --> 00:13:28,891
-You guys get at that end.
-[Jason] Alright.

307
00:13:29,683 --> 00:13:32,770
[Jason] Mary's asking 3.199 right now.

308
00:13:32,853 --> 00:13:33,813
So, 3.2 million.

309
00:13:33,896 --> 00:13:35,689
-Yeah, it ruins--
-Fits the style of the home.

310
00:13:35,773 --> 00:13:37,817
Yeah, it ruins the look, it blocks...

311
00:13:37,900 --> 00:13:38,984
They paid 1.7.

312
00:13:39,068 --> 00:13:42,404
Probably spent a couple hundred thousand
in carrying costs over the last two years.

313
00:13:42,488 --> 00:13:44,406
I think they spent a million 
just on remodel.

314
00:13:44,490 --> 00:13:46,659
So, right around three
is where they're into it.

315
00:13:46,742 --> 00:13:48,828
I cannot focus with Jason here.

316
00:13:48,911 --> 00:13:52,581
All I keep hearing is his voice.

317
00:13:52,665 --> 00:13:54,625
I keep focusing on them.

318
00:13:54,708 --> 00:13:57,378
I can't pay attention to my own client.

319
00:13:57,461 --> 00:13:59,463
Mary, sorry to interrupt, guys.

320
00:13:59,547 --> 00:14:02,883
Four bedrooms, three in the main house,
the fourth is the guest apartment.

321
00:14:02,967 --> 00:14:04,802
-[Mary] That's correct.
-Right? Okay.

322
00:14:04,885 --> 00:14:08,055
They're interested in leasing it out,
it'd be an investment for them.

323
00:14:08,138 --> 00:14:10,599
What do you think
a monthly long-term rental would be?

324
00:14:10,683 --> 00:14:14,019
I think furnished long-term,
it would be about 15,000 a month.

325
00:14:14,895 --> 00:14:15,813
-Okay.
-Alright.

326
00:14:15,896 --> 00:14:18,983
He's actually looking
for the same thing as well.

327
00:14:19,066 --> 00:14:19,984
Exactly.

328
00:14:20,067 --> 00:14:22,111
I think it rents for about 3,500 a month,

329
00:14:22,194 --> 00:14:24,530
so I don't think your numbers 
are gonna run.

330
00:14:24,947 --> 00:14:26,407
[Chris] Oh, darn. [laughing]

331
00:14:26,490 --> 00:14:27,783
-Alright, guys.
-Thanks, Mary.

332
00:14:27,867 --> 00:14:29,994
[Mary] He's pretty savvy,
he'll do his own numbers.

333
00:14:30,077 --> 00:14:32,246
-Thanks for that though, Jay. Good advice.
-You got it.

334
00:14:32,580 --> 00:14:34,748
As long as we get a great interest rate...

335
00:14:34,999 --> 00:14:37,084
And a good price. 
We also have to negotiate...

336
00:14:37,167 --> 00:14:39,587
[Mary] If you're looking
for an investment...

337
00:14:39,670 --> 00:14:42,756
Even though I own the brokerage,
I'm also an active real estate agent.

338
00:14:42,840 --> 00:14:43,966
It gets complicated.

339
00:14:44,049 --> 00:14:46,385
Technically, I'm on both sides 
of the transaction

340
00:14:46,468 --> 00:14:48,554
and I want to represent 
my agent's interests

341
00:14:48,637 --> 00:14:50,055
and my client's interests.

342
00:14:50,139 --> 00:14:53,183
Those are actually 
long-term clients of Jason's.

343
00:14:53,267 --> 00:14:56,729
They're legit, so if you're interested
we should probably get an offer in.

344
00:14:56,812 --> 00:14:58,439
-[Chris] Alright.
-Good seeing you.

345
00:14:58,522 --> 00:15:00,441
-You too.
-I'll give you a call later.

346
00:15:00,524 --> 00:15:01,734
You know what I want to pay.

347
00:15:01,817 --> 00:15:03,736
-[Jason laughing] Alright.
-[Amel] Bye.

348
00:15:04,862 --> 00:15:06,780
-[Mary] Well, that was surprising.
-Sorry--

349
00:15:06,864 --> 00:15:08,073
Yeah, sorry to barge in.

350
00:15:08,157 --> 00:15:10,034
I've been telling her about this house.

351
00:15:11,327 --> 00:15:14,330
She was really clear with me on pricing.

352
00:15:14,413 --> 00:15:16,749
-She thinks it's a little overpriced.
-It's not overpriced.

353
00:15:16,832 --> 00:15:20,544
It's a great location, but it is right on 
the street and the yard's a little small.

354
00:15:20,628 --> 00:15:22,880
Everything on Sunset Plaza 
is on the street.

355
00:15:23,505 --> 00:15:24,340
Oh, come on.

356
00:15:25,674 --> 00:15:30,262
I'm just telling you that Amel is not 
gonna write an offer you'll be happy with.

357
00:15:30,346 --> 00:15:31,513
If she even writes.

358
00:15:31,597 --> 00:15:33,474
So if you don't want to take it,
don't take it.

359
00:15:33,557 --> 00:15:35,517
Okay, well, I'm not going to be
concerned about it 

360
00:15:35,601 --> 00:15:37,811
until I get something 
offensive in writing, but...

361
00:15:38,479 --> 00:15:39,563
It's not gonna be offensive.

362
00:15:39,647 --> 00:15:42,232
If there's not a three in front of it,
it's pretty offensive.

363
00:15:42,316 --> 00:15:44,068
If it's 2.999, then it's not...

364
00:15:44,151 --> 00:15:47,196
It's not gonna be 2.9999999 either.

365
00:15:47,279 --> 00:15:51,533
It's totally embarrassing to take an offer
under three million to my client.

366
00:15:51,617 --> 00:15:53,786
Not just for me, but for the company.

367
00:15:53,869 --> 00:15:56,914
-When it's my seller--
-It's my job to represent her, not you.

368
00:15:56,997 --> 00:15:59,875
I'm not going to advise them
to take under market value. Why?

369
00:15:59,959 --> 00:16:02,419
-If we write an offer--
-You deal with your client and I mine.

370
00:16:02,503 --> 00:16:03,629
Don't stress me out anymore.

371
00:16:03,712 --> 00:16:05,547
I'm at my wit's end.

372
00:16:05,631 --> 00:16:08,759
This wedding is costing me so much money.

373
00:16:08,842 --> 00:16:11,136
We have to fly our families in,
try to get hotels.

374
00:16:11,220 --> 00:16:13,222
I'm doing everything I can.

375
00:16:13,514 --> 00:16:15,641
-[Mary sighs]
-What about that house on the beach?

376
00:16:15,724 --> 00:16:17,977
It's wonderful and it'll work,

377
00:16:18,060 --> 00:16:19,520
but there's still everything else.

378
00:16:19,603 --> 00:16:21,814
Romain just doesn't get it.
I'm working so hard--

379
00:16:21,897 --> 00:16:24,650
Don't yell at me, yell at Romain.

380
00:16:24,983 --> 00:16:25,818
I do.

381
00:16:25,901 --> 00:16:28,320
It's just hard. I know it's important.
I want him happy.

382
00:16:28,529 --> 00:16:29,738
I want his parents happy.

383
00:16:29,822 --> 00:16:30,656
I want like...

384
00:16:31,031 --> 00:16:32,700
I don't want to be mean, I don't want to

385
00:16:32,783 --> 00:16:35,369
make him feel
like I don't want to marry him.

386
00:16:35,452 --> 00:16:37,329
I do, a thousand percent.

387
00:16:37,413 --> 00:16:39,665
All this wedding-relationship talk...

388
00:16:39,748 --> 00:16:42,126
I think I'm getting a rash
or something like that.

389
00:16:42,251 --> 00:16:43,335
Oh my god.

390
00:16:43,419 --> 00:16:45,379
Oh... There is actually, yeah.

391
00:16:45,462 --> 00:16:46,755
You should go to the doctor.

392
00:16:54,680 --> 00:16:57,933
[Brett] Development properties are more
complicated than properties already built.

393
00:16:58,016 --> 00:17:02,104
It's a lot of pressure because I help
the developer buy the property.

394
00:17:02,187 --> 00:17:03,689
I run the numbers with them first

395
00:17:03,772 --> 00:17:05,566
and say, 
"You'll make money if you do this."

396
00:17:05,649 --> 00:17:07,401
I'm involved throughout 
the entire process.

397
00:17:07,484 --> 00:17:08,902
The funds come from the developer.

398
00:17:08,986 --> 00:17:10,571
If they don't make money, it's on me.

399
00:17:10,738 --> 00:17:12,448
-[Maya] Wow.
-[Brett] Yeah.

400
00:17:12,531 --> 00:17:14,700
[Maya] Don't go down. I have a son.

401
00:17:14,783 --> 00:17:17,202
[Brett] It doesn't matter if I die
because I'm single?

402
00:17:17,619 --> 00:17:20,289
It's still dirt, but it looks
so much different than last time.

403
00:17:20,372 --> 00:17:22,833
[Brett] Well, it's been a year.

404
00:17:22,916 --> 00:17:25,169
[Maya] How many square feet
is the basement?

405
00:17:25,252 --> 00:17:26,879
-6,500 square feet.
-Wow.

406
00:17:26,962 --> 00:17:27,880
14 ft deep.

407
00:17:27,963 --> 00:17:30,007
One of the biggest basements
built in Hollywood Hills.

408
00:17:30,090 --> 00:17:32,217
I can't believe that. 
When do you think it'll be ready?

409
00:17:33,135 --> 00:17:34,303
[Brett] 16 more months.

410
00:17:34,970 --> 00:17:37,389
[Maya] How often
can they dig the dirt out?

411
00:17:37,473 --> 00:17:39,975
[Brett] One week a month,
they let us take dirt out.

412
00:17:40,059 --> 00:17:41,852
Three weeks we're sitting on our ass.

413
00:17:41,935 --> 00:17:44,813
What do you do with the dirt?
Where do you take it? To Jason's house?

414
00:17:44,897 --> 00:17:46,690
-Jason's yard, yeah.
-[Maya laughing]

415
00:17:47,649 --> 00:17:49,735
Remember what you told me
last time you were here?

416
00:17:50,319 --> 00:17:52,613
Yeah, by the way I'm pregnant.
I'm kidding, no.

417
00:17:52,696 --> 00:17:53,864
You told me that last time.

418
00:17:53,947 --> 00:17:55,115
I know, last time.

419
00:17:55,199 --> 00:17:57,409
Will I crack the joke that 
I'm pregnant again? Not yet.

420
00:17:57,493 --> 00:17:58,494
Hopefully soon.

421
00:17:58,577 --> 00:18:01,455
What's crazy is you've had a baby
since the last time we were here.

422
00:18:01,538 --> 00:18:02,831
All we've done is dig a hole.

423
00:18:02,915 --> 00:18:04,124
I was busy.

424
00:18:04,208 --> 00:18:06,502
How long does it take to permit
something like this?

425
00:18:06,585 --> 00:18:09,379
I would say, with all the structural work,

426
00:18:09,463 --> 00:18:12,132
I'd say at least one and a half years,
two years?

427
00:18:12,216 --> 00:18:13,258
-[Brett] A year.
-Yeah.

428
00:18:13,342 --> 00:18:14,176
If you're good.

429
00:18:14,259 --> 00:18:16,845
What do you call it when it's completely
ready to go? Shovel ready?

430
00:18:16,929 --> 00:18:18,347
-RTI.
-Yes, RTI.

431
00:18:18,430 --> 00:18:19,973
-Damn, I'm good!
-Ready to issue.

432
00:18:20,057 --> 00:18:22,059
See, I was doing something
while I was pregnant.

433
00:18:22,142 --> 00:18:23,519
I'm learning and I'm reading.

434
00:18:23,602 --> 00:18:25,437
We should head down there.
You're in sneakers.

435
00:18:25,521 --> 00:18:28,690
Brett, if you want to hike with me,
you can take me to Runyon Canyon.

436
00:18:29,233 --> 00:18:30,567
-Shit!
-This is... Whoa!

437
00:18:30,651 --> 00:18:33,779
I can't break an ankle, I'm a mom,
I have responsibilities.

438
00:18:33,862 --> 00:18:35,531
-Wow.
-So, you're inside a basement.

439
00:18:35,614 --> 00:18:37,616
Now I really see the size of it. Huge!

440
00:18:37,699 --> 00:18:40,869
There's gonna be a huge tree right here
and you'll be able to see all the way up.

441
00:18:40,953 --> 00:18:44,289
I'd love to be able to sell a huge hole
in the ground for 25 million, but...

442
00:18:44,373 --> 00:18:46,750
-It's gonna be tough.
-I don't think I'm that good.

443
00:18:46,834 --> 00:18:49,253
I like that you're so into this,
that you're learning so much.

444
00:18:49,336 --> 00:18:51,755
-I like to get down and dirty.
-Yeah.

445
00:18:52,089 --> 00:18:53,590
[Maya] I've been working really hard 

446
00:18:53,674 --> 00:18:56,677
to understand deeply
the development process.

447
00:18:56,760 --> 00:18:58,971
It's a different transaction.

448
00:18:59,054 --> 00:19:01,598
And I like it because
you can make a lot of money.

449
00:19:02,349 --> 00:19:04,476
-Very productive day.
-[Brett] Woo!

450
00:19:06,019 --> 00:19:08,856
So yeah, maybe I'll co-list now with you.
What do you think?

451
00:19:09,815 --> 00:19:11,149
This one's my baby.

452
00:19:11,233 --> 00:19:13,777
-You have so many babies, Brett.
-I do, I have a lot.

453
00:19:14,444 --> 00:19:17,573
I do want to get you involved,
so we'll talk about that in the future.

454
00:19:18,407 --> 00:19:21,451
I'm a little disappointed.
Brett takes me to this tour,

455
00:19:21,535 --> 00:19:25,247
and I'm hoping maybe he's going
to put me as a co-list with him.

456
00:19:25,330 --> 00:19:28,000
He was just rubbing it in my face.
"Look at this property.

457
00:19:28,083 --> 00:19:31,128
Once I sell it, I'm going to make
a million dollars commission."

458
00:19:31,211 --> 00:19:32,671
I'm like, "Come on, Brett."

459
00:19:44,558 --> 00:19:49,187
This is my first solo,
my listing, open house.

460
00:19:49,271 --> 00:19:51,190
I got this listing through Jason.

461
00:19:51,273 --> 00:19:54,276
And it's really important that I sell it

462
00:19:54,359 --> 00:19:56,695
because I have two little kids to feed.

463
00:19:56,778 --> 00:19:57,821
I have a family.

464
00:20:20,344 --> 00:20:21,220
[grunts]

465
00:20:23,096 --> 00:20:23,972
Shoot!

466
00:20:24,056 --> 00:20:24,890
Argh!

467
00:20:27,893 --> 00:20:30,020
Okay, we're gonna pretend that works.

468
00:20:32,231 --> 00:20:35,734
[Mary] I'm so excited to see Amanza
in action at her first open house.

469
00:20:35,817 --> 00:20:38,195
And Jason may have asked me 
to check in on her.

470
00:20:40,489 --> 00:20:42,407
-Hey.
-[Amanza] Hi!

471
00:20:42,491 --> 00:20:44,618
-[Amanza] Are you house shopping?
-I am.

472
00:20:44,701 --> 00:20:46,995
You are? Will you buy this one from me?

473
00:20:47,079 --> 00:20:48,580
Well, tell me about it.

474
00:20:48,664 --> 00:20:50,624
-Do you have an agent?
-[both laughing]

475
00:20:50,874 --> 00:20:54,878
It's nice to see a friendly face. I really
appreciate that Mary's here to support me.

476
00:20:54,962 --> 00:20:56,755
-Hello, how's it going?
-How are you?

477
00:20:56,838 --> 00:20:57,756
-Amanza.
-Hi.

478
00:20:57,839 --> 00:21:00,050
-Charlie, nice to meet you.
-Nice to see you, Charlie.

479
00:21:00,133 --> 00:21:01,969
Hi, I'm Amanza's colleague.

480
00:21:02,094 --> 00:21:04,721
-Great to meet you.
-I just stopped in to check on her.

481
00:21:04,805 --> 00:21:05,764
Just to say hi.

482
00:21:05,847 --> 00:21:07,432
Do you live in the area?

483
00:21:07,516 --> 00:21:08,809
-I do.
-Currently? You do?

484
00:21:08,892 --> 00:21:10,310
Yeah, new to LA.

485
00:21:10,394 --> 00:21:12,020
Okay, are you looking to buy?

486
00:21:12,104 --> 00:21:14,398
Or just curious to see
what's for sale in the neighborhood?

487
00:21:14,481 --> 00:21:15,315
Looking to buy.

488
00:21:15,440 --> 00:21:17,943
[Amanza] What are you looking for?
Do you know square footage?

489
00:21:18,026 --> 00:21:19,069
What's your budget?

490
00:21:19,152 --> 00:21:21,488
Definitely need a pool, so check.

491
00:21:22,447 --> 00:21:24,408
Have a look around.
If you have any questions,

492
00:21:24,866 --> 00:21:25,867
-I'm here.
-Thank you.

493
00:21:27,119 --> 00:21:28,328
Sorry, excuse me.

494
00:21:28,412 --> 00:21:30,330
So, what's the square footage?

495
00:21:30,414 --> 00:21:31,832
And when was this built?

496
00:21:31,915 --> 00:21:33,458
[Amanza] That's a good question.

497
00:21:33,542 --> 00:21:35,127
How long has it been on the market?

498
00:21:35,210 --> 00:21:36,086
Um, I don't know.

499
00:21:36,169 --> 00:21:40,132
[Amanza] I was studying this 
before you walked in the door.

500
00:21:40,215 --> 00:21:42,718
Are you giving everyone
those set of sheets when they come in?

501
00:21:42,801 --> 00:21:44,803
Yeah... at some point.

502
00:21:45,554 --> 00:21:47,055
How many bedrooms is it?

503
00:21:47,139 --> 00:21:50,142
It's three bedrooms, three baths.
Here, I'll give you a sheet.

504
00:21:50,517 --> 00:21:52,644
Just seeing all these people face-to-face

505
00:21:52,728 --> 00:21:55,355
is giving me, like, massive anxiety. Um...

506
00:21:55,731 --> 00:21:57,232
My mind is going blank.

507
00:21:57,316 --> 00:21:59,943
I just, I never had 
to do this as a stager.

508
00:22:00,027 --> 00:22:01,611
[Mary whispers] You're doing great.

509
00:22:01,945 --> 00:22:03,405
[quietly] Thank you, I'm sweating.

510
00:22:10,912 --> 00:22:13,874
[woman] I've known you forever 
so I'm so happy to hear that.

511
00:22:15,042 --> 00:22:16,585
-Oh!
-Hi!

512
00:22:16,668 --> 00:22:19,254
[Mary] What are you doing here?
There's so many people.

513
00:22:19,338 --> 00:22:21,465
-Good to see you.
-Are you doing what I'm doing?

514
00:22:21,548 --> 00:22:23,550
Yeah, it's a little bit misleading.

515
00:22:23,633 --> 00:22:26,136
[woman] I did not expect all of this
when I walked in.

516
00:22:26,219 --> 00:22:27,179
I was gonna say...

517
00:22:27,471 --> 00:22:29,723
Hi! Who's this?

518
00:22:29,806 --> 00:22:31,850
-[man] This is Alexa.
-[Amanza] Hi, Alexa.

519
00:22:31,933 --> 00:22:33,685
-Say, "Hi."
-How are you today?

520
00:22:34,227 --> 00:22:36,229
Are you helping Daddy look for a house?

521
00:22:36,772 --> 00:22:37,939
-[man] Yes.
-Yeah?

522
00:22:38,023 --> 00:22:40,734
She'll be good with these buyers

523
00:22:40,817 --> 00:22:42,152
'cause she's so good with kids.

524
00:22:42,235 --> 00:22:45,947
-Let me grab you a sheet on the house.
-Okay.

525
00:22:46,031 --> 00:22:48,200
It took me a minute, but I do learn.

526
00:22:48,617 --> 00:22:49,826
[chuckling]

527
00:22:49,910 --> 00:22:51,161
[man] What do we have here?

528
00:22:51,244 --> 00:22:53,705
-This is so nice out here.
-[man] Wow, it's beautiful.

529
00:22:53,789 --> 00:22:54,790
It's peaceful.

530
00:22:54,873 --> 00:22:56,625
You've got the outdoor dining.

531
00:22:56,708 --> 00:22:59,086
Do you want to see the fish?
There's fish

532
00:22:59,169 --> 00:23:01,379
-in the water here.
-Do you want to go with her?

533
00:23:01,922 --> 00:23:03,006
Come here.

534
00:23:03,757 --> 00:23:04,591
Okay.

535
00:23:05,008 --> 00:23:06,468
[Amanza laughing]

536
00:23:06,551 --> 00:23:08,553
I would like to have my wife
come and look at this.

537
00:23:08,637 --> 00:23:09,471
Yeah, for sure.

538
00:23:09,554 --> 00:23:12,766
And maybe if you have a card or something,
I can contact you.

539
00:23:12,849 --> 00:23:14,518
-Well, thank you so much.
-Thank you.

540
00:23:14,601 --> 00:23:16,144
-See you soon.
-Bye, Alexa.

541
00:23:16,228 --> 00:23:17,646
She's like such a mama bear.

542
00:23:17,729 --> 00:23:18,730
I know.

543
00:23:19,022 --> 00:23:20,273
That's so cute

544
00:23:20,357 --> 00:23:22,067
[Amanza] How cute was that little girl?

545
00:23:22,150 --> 00:23:23,819
[Chrishell] So cute.

546
00:23:23,944 --> 00:23:25,320
-She was adorable.
-The cutest.

547
00:23:25,404 --> 00:23:27,072
I kinda wanted to kidnap her.

548
00:23:27,155 --> 00:23:29,408
That might have been a little awkward.

549
00:23:29,491 --> 00:23:32,369
Honestly, it's a great house,
it's a great location.

550
00:23:32,452 --> 00:23:34,704
-[Amanza] I'd buy it.
-It's priced really well.

551
00:23:34,788 --> 00:23:37,207
I don't think you're going to have
an issue selling the house.

552
00:23:37,290 --> 00:23:38,917
[Mary] You're doing really well, hon.

553
00:23:39,000 --> 00:23:41,044
I just wanted to tell you, 
we've been watching...

554
00:23:41,128 --> 00:23:42,295
How are you feeling?

555
00:23:42,379 --> 00:23:44,756
With everything that went down.
You feeling good with Heather?

556
00:23:44,840 --> 00:23:48,301
It terrifies me how fast
you have met those kids.

557
00:23:48,385 --> 00:23:50,887
I'm glad you're worried about
my boyfriend's children, thank you.

558
00:23:50,971 --> 00:23:54,266
If I thought that you were going to be 
this angry at me for saying it,

559
00:23:54,349 --> 00:23:55,851
-I would have kept my mouth shut.
-Good.

560
00:23:57,477 --> 00:23:58,562
Oh. [scoffs]

561
00:23:58,645 --> 00:24:00,689
Because I know you guys
needed to talk it out.

562
00:24:00,772 --> 00:24:03,984
-So it felt like it went well.
-I guess, I don't know.

563
00:24:04,067 --> 00:24:05,819
I felt that day like it was fine.

564
00:24:05,902 --> 00:24:06,736
But...

565
00:24:07,112 --> 00:24:11,074
I've so many other major life things
going on that I honestly...

566
00:24:11,158 --> 00:24:12,492
[Mary] Everything okay?

567
00:24:12,868 --> 00:24:14,077
I'll sit here.

568
00:24:14,786 --> 00:24:15,662
What's wrong?

569
00:24:15,745 --> 00:24:17,289
[Amanza] Like, about the kids.

570
00:24:17,747 --> 00:24:21,501
I don't know what it is, but I feel
like I'm gonna maybe have to...

571
00:24:22,169 --> 00:24:23,128
Um...

572
00:24:23,503 --> 00:24:25,672
Like, get full custody of them.

573
00:24:25,755 --> 00:24:27,215
Oh my God.

574
00:24:27,340 --> 00:24:32,220
At this point, legally we still have
50-50, but I don't know where he is,

575
00:24:32,304 --> 00:24:34,806
so I need to be able to make decisions

576
00:24:35,348 --> 00:24:39,895
without his signature, his approval,
because it's impossible right now.

577
00:24:39,978 --> 00:24:42,981
So, I have a court date set 
in a couple of weeks.

578
00:24:43,064 --> 00:24:44,191
[chuckles awkwardly]

579
00:24:45,066 --> 00:24:46,109
What happened?

580
00:24:46,193 --> 00:24:49,112
I mean, he's not doing anything 
bad to them, but it's...

581
00:24:49,487 --> 00:24:51,656
I'm just like, you know.

582
00:24:51,740 --> 00:24:55,035
My kids are like my world
 and if they're not okay,

583
00:24:55,118 --> 00:24:56,328
Mommy's not okay.

584
00:24:56,536 --> 00:24:59,372
Yesterday, they just didn't seem
like they were okay.

585
00:24:59,456 --> 00:25:00,582
Noah was sad.

586
00:25:00,665 --> 00:25:03,960
-Honey, you've been going through so much.
-[Amanza] It's okay, I know.

587
00:25:04,044 --> 00:25:06,296
Right now, I'm a little bit overwhelmed.

588
00:25:06,379 --> 00:25:09,299
If you need any help,
I'm obviously here.

589
00:25:09,382 --> 00:25:10,675
You love to babysit.

590
00:25:10,759 --> 00:25:15,055
Did you just hear her say,
"I'll babysit anytime. I love kids."

591
00:25:15,847 --> 00:25:16,765
[Mary] Okay.

592
00:25:16,848 --> 00:25:18,475
[dragonfly buzzing]

593
00:25:19,059 --> 00:25:20,185
[dragonflies buzzing]

594
00:25:20,268 --> 00:25:21,520
What the fuck?

595
00:25:21,937 --> 00:25:23,605
Oh my God! What is that?

596
00:25:24,731 --> 00:25:26,650
-Look out behind you!
-[Mary yells]

597
00:25:26,733 --> 00:25:28,735
[Chrishell] Oh my god, that scared me.

598
00:25:29,236 --> 00:25:30,195
What was that?

599
00:25:30,278 --> 00:25:32,280
It's a dragonfly, I think, right?

600
00:25:32,364 --> 00:25:34,407
Maybe dragonflies are good luck?

601
00:25:34,491 --> 00:25:36,701
No, it's if a bird shits on you,
it's good luck.

602
00:25:36,785 --> 00:25:38,036
I think both.

603
00:25:38,119 --> 00:25:39,371
Let's take it as a good sign.

604
00:25:39,454 --> 00:25:41,373
-[Mary] I like that.
-Get the heck out of here.

605
00:25:41,456 --> 00:25:42,791
-[phone ringing]
-[Mary] Hello?

606
00:25:42,874 --> 00:25:44,125
Shawn Elliot, how are you?

607
00:25:44,209 --> 00:25:45,710
I'm good. How are you?

608
00:25:45,794 --> 00:25:50,549
[Shawn sighs] Unfortunately,
the owners of Il Pelicano

609
00:25:50,632 --> 00:25:52,968
are in the midst of a divorce.

610
00:25:53,593 --> 00:25:56,972
I guess the wife was all for the wedding

611
00:25:57,389 --> 00:25:59,224
and the husband's not on the same page.

612
00:25:59,933 --> 00:26:04,062
So, I'm really sorry to tell you
that, uh...

613
00:26:04,145 --> 00:26:06,690
-[Mary] Oh my God.
-...you'll have to look for another venue.

614
00:26:06,773 --> 00:26:07,941
Thank you for letting me know.

615
00:26:08,024 --> 00:26:09,776
-[Shawn] Of course.
-[Mary] Okay, bye.

616
00:26:11,111 --> 00:26:12,070
Okay, but...

617
00:26:12,737 --> 00:26:15,490
Think about it this way,
we can find another spot.

618
00:26:15,573 --> 00:26:17,701
-[Amanza] We just said that.
-Are you kidding me?

619
00:26:17,784 --> 00:26:18,618
[Amanza] Okay.

620
00:26:18,910 --> 00:26:20,662
My wedding's in five weeks.

621
00:26:24,874 --> 00:26:28,295
♪ We're gonna do this
Like, like we do this ♪

622
00:26:28,378 --> 00:26:30,589
♪ Ain't nobody else can do this ♪

623
00:26:30,672 --> 00:26:32,299
♪ Like us, like us ♪

624
00:26:33,717 --> 00:26:36,428
Hey Laura, it's Brett Oppenheim.
A quick question for you.

625
00:26:36,511 --> 00:26:38,972
I'm looking at the pictures of your-- Oh!

626
00:26:39,306 --> 00:26:41,641
Gosh, it's the wrong building,
never mind. I was gonna ask...

627
00:26:41,725 --> 00:26:43,184
See it's not my building, Jesus.

628
00:26:43,268 --> 00:26:44,811
[Jason] I didn't say it was.

629
00:26:44,894 --> 00:26:46,187
-[Brett] Never mind.
-I'm tired.

630
00:26:46,271 --> 00:26:49,399
Everyday I wake up at 5:30 a.m.
because Aiden is waking up.

631
00:26:49,482 --> 00:26:52,527
[Heather] That's how I feel
being a stepmom, honestly.

632
00:26:52,610 --> 00:26:54,738
A mom's job is hard. [laughing]

633
00:26:55,572 --> 00:26:57,449
Yeah, it's a lot. I mean...

634
00:26:57,532 --> 00:26:59,326
Yeah. I mean, I love it though.

635
00:26:59,743 --> 00:27:01,536
I love it. It's just, um...

636
00:27:02,537 --> 00:27:04,539
It doesn't stop. It doesn't stop.

637
00:27:04,622 --> 00:27:05,832
[Maya] No, it doesn't.

638
00:27:06,374 --> 00:27:09,127
Yeah, talk to me when you're
running on one hour's sleep,

639
00:27:09,210 --> 00:27:11,046
holding a crying baby,

640
00:27:11,129 --> 00:27:12,672
and you're covered with spit.

641
00:27:12,756 --> 00:27:13,757
Talk to me then.

642
00:27:13,840 --> 00:27:17,802
It's just making me realize,
I don't think I want my own.

643
00:27:17,969 --> 00:27:18,845
[Maya] Really?

644
00:27:18,928 --> 00:27:21,222
If anyone gets anything off market
in Santa Monica,

645
00:27:21,306 --> 00:27:23,975
-around three, send it to me.
-[Heather] Where in Santa Monica?

646
00:27:24,059 --> 00:27:26,561
It all sells pocket listing.
Anytime, let me know.

647
00:27:26,645 --> 00:27:28,313
[Heather] I'm so out of the loop.

648
00:27:28,396 --> 00:27:30,273
I can't even hear what's going on.

649
00:27:30,357 --> 00:27:31,733
I'm not going to say anything then.

650
00:27:34,319 --> 00:27:35,904
[cell phone ringing]

651
00:27:36,529 --> 00:27:38,114
Christine, why are you FaceTiming me?

652
00:27:38,198 --> 00:27:41,409
I'm FaceTiming you because I can't talk 
to you, you're all the way back there.

653
00:27:41,493 --> 00:27:43,203
It's the only way I can talk. Answer.

654
00:27:43,286 --> 00:27:44,287
[Heather] Oh, hi.

655
00:27:44,371 --> 00:27:46,081
[Christine] Listen. I have a buyer

656
00:27:46,164 --> 00:27:50,251
who's looking for something
below 2.5 up in the Hills.

657
00:27:50,794 --> 00:27:52,837
You guys, this is for you guys, too.

658
00:27:52,921 --> 00:27:54,506
[Heather] He wants up to 2.5?

659
00:27:55,298 --> 00:27:56,633
Up to 2.5, 2.7 maybe.

660
00:27:56,758 --> 00:27:59,052
I just wanted to relay
that information to you.

661
00:27:59,135 --> 00:28:01,429
-Thank you, babe.
-Okay, keep me posted.

662
00:28:01,513 --> 00:28:03,515
-Okay, bye.
-[Heather] Bye.

663
00:28:03,723 --> 00:28:05,642
So, let me know, guys.
I'm looking for a buyer.

664
00:28:05,725 --> 00:28:08,103
[Amanza] Mary! Hi.

665
00:28:08,186 --> 00:28:11,314
-[Brett] Did Frederick's team get back?
-[Jason] No, they're at Burning Man.

666
00:28:11,398 --> 00:28:12,732
[Amanza] What's going on?

667
00:28:12,816 --> 00:28:14,192
Kill me. Oh my God.

668
00:28:14,275 --> 00:28:15,193
Guys, what's going on?

669
00:28:15,276 --> 00:28:17,904
-The wife is still, um...
-[Heather] I'm coming.

670
00:28:17,987 --> 00:28:19,114
[Heather] What's going on?

671
00:28:19,197 --> 00:28:20,740
Our wedding venue fell through.

672
00:28:21,157 --> 00:28:22,367
[Mary] The Malibu house.

673
00:28:22,450 --> 00:28:23,576
[Maya] Really? Why?

674
00:28:24,035 --> 00:28:25,662
The owners are getting a divorce.

675
00:28:25,745 --> 00:28:27,580
-I thought it was set.
-[Mary sighs]

676
00:28:27,664 --> 00:28:30,417
-What's your other options?
-[Mary] I have no idea.

677
00:28:30,500 --> 00:28:34,129
I don't know what to do
because our family members

678
00:28:34,212 --> 00:28:35,505
have booked their flights.

679
00:28:35,588 --> 00:28:36,631
-They did?
-Are you serious?

680
00:28:36,715 --> 00:28:38,258
Yeah, from France.

681
00:28:38,341 --> 00:28:40,051
Do you have other back-up places?

682
00:28:40,135 --> 00:28:41,970
-[Maya] The office.
-We're reaching back out.

683
00:28:42,053 --> 00:28:44,681
What, we have five weeks?
Less than that.

684
00:28:44,764 --> 00:28:47,642
I'm torn between pushing it back

685
00:28:47,726 --> 00:28:49,436
and being like,
"why are we doing this?"

686
00:28:49,519 --> 00:28:51,146
Romain and I are fighting all the time.

687
00:28:51,229 --> 00:28:53,940
I would rather... not do it.

688
00:28:58,278 --> 00:29:00,321
-[Chrishell] Oh, don't...
-[Amanza] Don't cry.

689
00:29:00,405 --> 00:29:03,408
Mary, I think Christine said she'll do
a joint wedding with you.

690
00:29:03,491 --> 00:29:05,243
You guys can get married together.

691
00:29:05,326 --> 00:29:07,662
You're at 5 p.m. and she's at 7 p.m.

692
00:29:07,745 --> 00:29:08,955
There you go.

693
00:29:09,038 --> 00:29:10,540
[Amanza] I wanna get married, too.

694
00:29:10,623 --> 00:29:13,376
-[Maya] Two birds with one.
-You can always get married at Jason's.

695
00:29:13,460 --> 00:29:16,004
[Maya] I think Romain would rather
get married at my apartment.

696
00:29:16,087 --> 00:29:18,465
There's no consummating 
the marriage at my house.

697
00:29:18,548 --> 00:29:21,384
-[Amanza] Ew, creepy.
-[Mary] I hate that word, consummating.

698
00:29:21,468 --> 00:29:22,761
Sounds like constipated.

699
00:29:22,844 --> 00:29:25,388
-I have that problem, too.
-[Jason] You know what we can do?

700
00:29:25,513 --> 00:29:27,932
-We have a, uh...
-[women talking at once]

701
00:29:28,016 --> 00:29:29,434
-One at a time.
-God, I know.

702
00:29:29,517 --> 00:29:30,393
[Heather] Do a big...

703
00:29:30,477 --> 00:29:33,104
-Do a restaurant, rent a big room.
-[Chrishell] Big reception party?

704
00:29:33,188 --> 00:29:34,105
Hey, Lizzie.

705
00:29:34,189 --> 00:29:38,026
I was wondering if you had any thoughts
on Mary's wedding venue. Question mark.

706
00:29:38,443 --> 00:29:42,447
Lizzie is Mary's client, but Mary
often brings me on to her listings.

707
00:29:42,697 --> 00:29:44,741
So I've gotten to know Lizzie very well.

708
00:29:44,824 --> 00:29:48,203
I thought it would be a good idea just
to kind of put the bug in Lizzie's ear

709
00:29:48,286 --> 00:29:50,997
and see if she'd be open 
to Mary getting married there.

710
00:29:51,080 --> 00:29:53,082
[Chrishell] I feel we should
just rent a yacht

711
00:29:53,166 --> 00:29:54,709
and do it on a boat.

712
00:29:54,793 --> 00:29:56,836
I know. Who's got a yacht?

713
00:29:56,920 --> 00:29:59,297
